//! HTTP Client Library with Retry Logic
//!
//! This library provides a typed HTTP client with retry logic, TLS/mTLS support,
//! and integration with proto types.
//!
//! # Architecture
//!
//! The package provides three main components:
//!
//! 1. **TypedClient** - A wrapper around reqwest::Client with configured TLS, timeouts, and connection pooling
//! 2. **Static helper functions** - Generic functions for GET plus single-attempt POST and mutations
//! 3. **RetryConfig** - Configuration for jittered exponential backoff retry behavior
//!
//! # Features
//!
//! - **Retry Logic**: Automatic retry with jittered exponential backoff for failed requests
//! - **TLS/mTLS Support**: Configure custom root CAs and client certificates
//! - **Connection Pooling**: Configure connection pool settings
//! - **Typed Errors**: Returns proto error types
//! - **Debug/Trace Logging**: Detailed logging at debug and trace levels
//!
//! # Retry Logic
//!
//! Read-like HTTP operations support automatic retry with jittered exponential backoff:
//! - GET/HEAD/OPTIONS may retry network errors
//! - HTTP status codes can be configured as retryable (default: 429, 500, 502, 503, 504)
//! - Backoff starts at 100ms and doubles each retry (configurable)
//! - Maximum backoff is capped at 5 seconds (configurable)
//! - Default maximum retries is 3 (configurable)
//! - POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are single-attempt by default to avoid duplicate side effects
//!
//! # Debug and Trace Logging
//!
//! The library provides two levels of logging:
//!
//! **Debug Level** (always logged at debug):
//! - Request method, URL, attempt number, and status code
//!
//! **Trace Level** (only when trace logging is enabled):
//! - Request body (for POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE)
//! - Response body
//!
//! # Example Usage
//!
//! ```rust
//! use httpclient::{TypedClient, ClientError};
//! use {{.CrateBasePathUnderscore}}_types::sys::httpclient::HttpClientConfig;
//!
//! #[tokio::main]
//! async fn main() -> Result<(), ClientError> {
//!     // Create client with default retry config
//!     let config = HttpClientConfig {
//!         timeout_seconds: 30,
//!         max_idle_conns: 100,
//!         ..Default::default()
//!     };
//!
//!     let client = TypedClient::new(Some(&config))?;
//!
//!     // Use the client for requests
//!     // (Generated code will call do_get, do_post_with_response, do_mutation)
//!
//!     Ok(())
//! }
//! ```

